From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 09:45:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cmake: find TBB in the openvino wheel's flat cmake dir

The riscv64 openvino wheel from pypi.riseproject.dev is built against a
oneTBB compiled from source and passed in with -DTBB_DIR, because the
prebuilt riscv64 oneTBB that openvino downloads targets T-Head cores only.
openvino's install_tbb.cmake treats such a TBB as "custom" and records
OV_TBB_DIR_INSTALL as runtime/3rdparty/tbb/lib/cmake/TBB, which the wheel's
setup.py then rewrites to <openvino>/cmake/lib/cmake/TBB while flattening
TBBConfig.cmake and friends into <openvino>/cmake. The wheel's
OpenVINOConfig.cmake therefore fails find_package(OpenVINO COMPONENTS
Threading) with:

  CMake Error at .../openvino/cmake/OpenVINOConfig.cmake:119 (message):
    File or directory
    .../openvino/cmake/lib/cmake/TBB
    referenced by variable _tbb_dir does not exist !

The PyPI x86_64 wheel bundles the downloaded TBB instead, so its
_tbb_dir is <openvino>/cmake and the build works there.

When the wheel ships TBBConfig.cmake flat and the nested directory is
missing, create it so set_and_check() passes, and point TBB_DIR at the
flat directory so find_package(TBB) loads the config from where its
relative import paths resolve to <site-packages>/openvino/libs.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [works around the packaging of our riscv64 openvino wheel, built with a custom oneTBB]
---
 CMakeLists.txt | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index c722713..d28c974 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -80,6 +80,10 @@ if(BUILD_CPP_EXTENSION)
                  COMPONENTS Runtime Threading
                  PATHS "${OpenVINO_DIR}")
     if(NOT OpenVINODeveloperPackage_FOUND)
+        if(OpenVINO_DIR_PY AND EXISTS "${OpenVINO_DIR_PY}/TBBConfig.cmake" AND NOT EXISTS "${OpenVINO_DIR_PY}/lib/cmake/TBB")
+            file(MAKE_DIRECTORY "${OpenVINO_DIR_PY}/lib/cmake/TBB")
+            set(TBB_DIR "${OpenVINO_DIR_PY}" CACHE PATH "Directory containing TBBConfig.cmake")
+        endif()
         find_package(OpenVINO ${OV_COMPATIBILITY_VERSION} REQUIRED
                      COMPONENTS Runtime Threading
                      PATHS "${OpenVINO_DIR_PY}")
--
